| **Name**                                     |                               **Type / How to get** | **What it gives / How to use it**                                                                                    | **Example (one-line)**                                                                   |
| -------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------: | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `hit.collider`                               |                 `Collider collider = hit.collider;` | The collider that was hit. Use to read tag, layer, component, or PhysicMaterial.                                     | `if(hit.collider.CompareTag("Enemy")) Kill(hit.collider.gameObject);`                    |
| `hit.transform`                              |                      `Transform t = hit.transform;` | The `Transform` of the hit object (null-safe). Convenient for parenting or reading position/rotation.                | `t.Rotate(...);`                                                                         |
| `hit.rigidbody`                              |                     `Rigidbody rb = hit.rigidbody;` | The `Rigidbody` attached to collider (if any). Use to apply forces or impulses.                                      | `rb?.AddForceAtPosition(ray.direction*force, hit.point, ForceMode.Impulse);`             |
| `hit.point`                                  |                            `Vector3 p = hit.point;` | Exact world position of the hit. Use to spawn effects, place objects, compute movement target.                       | `Instantiate(impactFX, hit.point, Quaternion.identity);`                                 |
| `hit.normal`                                 |                           `Vector3 n = hit.normal;` | Surface normal at hit point. Use to align decals, orient objects, compute reflection.                                | `var rot = Quaternion.LookRotation(-n);`                                                 |
| `hit.distance`                               |                           `float d = hit.distance;` | Distance from ray origin to hit point. Useful for range checks and UI display.                                       | `if(hit.distance < maxRange) ...`                                                        |
| `hit.collider.sharedMaterial`                |  `PhysicMaterial pm = hit.collider.sharedMaterial;` | Physical surface properties (friction, bounciness). Useful for sound or physics tweaks.                              | `PlaySoundForMaterial(pm);`                                                              |
| `hit.textureCoord`                           |                    `Vector2 uv = hit.textureCoord;` | UV coordinates on the mesh at the hit point. Useful for painting/decals on textured meshes.                          | `Color c = sampleTextureAt(uv);`                                                         |
| `hit.textureCoord2`                          |                  `Vector2 uv2 = hit.textureCoord2;` | Second UV set (lightmaps or custom). Use for advanced decals or lightmap mapping.                                    | `// use for lightmap-aware decals`                                                       |
| `hit.lightmapCoord`                          |                 `Vector2 lmUV = hit.lightmapCoord;` | UVs in the lightmap; needed when placing lightmap-aware decals.                                                      | `// compute decal placement in lightmap space`                                           |
| `hit.triangleIndex`                          |                      `int tri = hit.triangleIndex;` | Index of triangle hit in the mesh. Use to get exact triangle vertices for advanced deformation/painting.             | `var mesh = GetMeshFromCollider(hit.collider); var indices = mesh.triangles[tri*3 ...];` |
| `hit.barycentricCoordinate`                  |            `Vector3 b = hit.barycentricCoordinate;` | Barycentric weights inside the hit triangle — helpful to interpolate vertex attributes (colors/normals).             | `var interpolated = v0*b.x + v1*b.y + v2*b.z;`                                           |
| `Physics.RaycastAll(...)`                    |      `RaycastHit[] hits = Physics.RaycastAll(ray);` | Returns *all* hits along ray sorted by distance (unsorted pre-Unity 2020). Use when you need multiple intersections. | `foreach(var h in hits) Process(h);`                                                     |
| `Physics.RaycastNonAlloc(...)`               |     `int n = Physics.RaycastNonAlloc(ray, buffer);` | Fills preallocated array (no GC). Use inside Update to avoid allocations.                                            | `int count = Physics.RaycastNonAlloc(ray, results, range);`                              |
| `Collider.Raycast(ray, out hit, maxDist)`    |  `collider.Raycast(ray, out RaycastHit h, maxDist)` | Raycast against a *specific* collider. Use for custom checks against one object only.                                | `if(myCollider.Raycast(ray, out var h, 10f)) ...`                                        |
| `Physics.SphereCast / BoxCast / CapsuleCast` | `Physics.SphereCast(ray, radius, out hit, maxDist)` | Cast a volume rather than a single line — useful for wider sensors and avoiding tunneling.                           | `Physics.SphereCast(ray, 0.5f, out hit, 10f)`                                            |
